  "change": "Add exact volatile operation tokens and receiver retirement. Cancel invokes one error callback/context release, retains execution slot until original completion or explicit view close; manual activity follows the same separation. Late callbacks cannot publish content/observation identity or touch a successor.",
  "api": {
    "starts": "ff_browser_read/observe/act take nonzero operation_id immediately after browser id. Caller must never reuse it in the process.",
    "cancel": "bool ff_browser_cancel_operation(browser_id,operation_id). true only means matching receiver retired (idempotent); it is NOT proof JavaScript stopped or action had no effect. false means no exact match, not success/cancellation proof.",
    "zeroUnknown": "Zero/unknown browser/unknown operation do not touch the request. A rejected start never invokes its callback; caller retains the Box.",
    "ownership": "Started request callback is sole context owner. finish nulls callback/context before invocation for reentrancy. Cancel keeps request object pending. Completion clears only the same request. Close clears this view and does not affect same-id replacement.",
    "readAdmission": "Until actual pending execution completes, follow-up Read/Observe/Act remain busy. An unending operation can be recovered by explicit close, not automatic reload/retry.",
    "alreadyDispatched": "Cancellation/timeout is unknown effect. An actual controlled click demonstrates the page can change after its receiver retires."
  },
